  "knowledgePattern": "Recover a binomial exponent from consecutive coefficient ratios",
  "knowledgeTags": [
    "algebra"
  ],
  "solution": "<p>Write the three coefficients as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"0\"><mi>n</mi><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"0\"><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"0\"><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>. Their adjacent ratios are 3 and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>, not 3 and 5.</p><p>Using the factorial formula, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>. The first gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>. Substitute this into the second: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>, hence <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p>Checking the row, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"0\"><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"0\"><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>21</mn></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"0\"><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>35</mn></mrow></math>, with the required ratio 1:3:5. Answer B.</p>",
